import DocsLayout from "../../layouts/DocsLayout.astro";

const admissionCode = `let ids = AgentRunIds::generate();
// Persist external_idempotency_key -> ids before the first attempt.

let request = DurableAgentAdmissionRequest::new(
    tenant_id,
    ids,
    agent_descriptor,
    agent_request,
    evaluated_budget_layers,
    graph_reference,
    admission_authority,
    initial_state,
)?;

let retry_bytes = serde_json::to_vec(&request)?;
let outcome = admission.admit(request).await?;`;
---

<DocsLayout
  title="Admit one Agent as an atomic durable fact."
  description="Validate one authenticated Agent intent and atomically commit its database-clock admission, first event, initial checkpoint, Active lifecycle, and scheduler visibility."
  section="Durable Agent admission"
>
  <aside class="docs-callout" aria-labelledby="admission-boundary-title">
    <h2 id="admission-boundary-title">Implemented admission, pre-alpha API</h2>
    <p>
      <code>DurableAgentAdmission</code>, migration 15, and the immutable Core
      admission contract are implemented. They close the partial-initialization
      gap. The public run/result facade and ingress idempotency store are now
      implemented separately; this page keeps the exact-ID lower boundary clear.
      The implemented <a href="/docs/provider-native-agent/"
        >provider-native Agent graph</a
      > consumes this immutable admission above the lower boundary.
    </p>
  </aside>

  <section aria-labelledby="transaction-title">
    <h2 id="transaction-title">Commit the executable boundary once</h2>
    <p>
      One PostgreSQL transaction stores the authenticated Agent, request,
      policy, granted scopes, finite budget, graph, and database time together
      with the sequence-one <code>agent-admitted</code> event, superstep-zero checkpoint,
      Active lifecycle, and every scheduler projection. No worker can claim the run
      between those writes.
    </p>
    <p>
      The revised scheduler index requires an initial checkpoint. The legacy
      low-level <code>admit_run</code> API therefore creates an addressable but scheduler-invisible
      row; new Agent ingress must use the atomic facade.
    </p>
  </section>

  <section aria-labelledby="deployment-title">
    <h2 id="deployment-title">Freeze every dependency before traffic</h2>
    <p>
      Register the standard admission, Graph Driver, and lifecycle schemas plus
      every application schema before freezing one executable registry. Install
      the exact graph/reducer/node closure locally and register the same
      compiled graph for the tenant in PostgreSQL. A retry requires that
      digest-pinned deployment to remain available.
    </p>
    <p>
      The public-safe admission event schema is published at <a
        href="/schemas/runtime/agent-admission-event/1.0.0"
        ><code
          >https://stknot.com/schemas/runtime/agent-admission-event/1.0.0</code
        ></a
      >. Register it through <code
        >register_standard_agent_admission_event_schema</code
      > instead of pinning a copied digest.
    </p>
  </section>

  <section aria-labelledby="request-title">
    <h2 id="request-title">Retain exact retry authority</h2>
    <p>
      Authenticate the principal and evaluate the immutable policy outside this
      facade. Internal callers of <code>admit</code> allocate one complete
      <code>AgentRunIds</code> bundle and retain the request bytes; a timeout must
      reuse all five IDs. User-facing ingress should instead use <a
        href="/docs/runs/"><code>DurableAgentRuns::submit</code></a
      >, which persists the key mapping and permits fresh candidate IDs.
    </p>
    <div class="docs-code" data-code-block>
      <div class="docs-code-head">
        <span>Rust · trusted ingress</span>
        <button
          class="copy-button affordance"
          type="button"
          data-copy-button
          data-copy-target="agent-admission-code"
        >
          <span data-copy-label aria-live="polite">Copy</span>
        </button>
      </div>
      <pre
        id="agent-admission-code"
        tabindex="0"><code>{admissionCode}</code></pre>
    </div>
    <p>
      An ambiguous retry probes and verifies committed evidence before applying
      the current database clock, so an exact request can converge after its
      original deadline. Changed input, policy, budget, graph, initial state,
      ready set, event, checkpoint, or identity is a conflict—not a second run.
    </p>
  </section>

  <section aria-labelledby="validation-title">
    <h2 id="validation-title">Reject drift before mutation</h2>
    <ol class="evidence-list">
      <li>
        <h3>Resolve code</h3>
        <p>
          Require the exact executable graph and exact Agent-to-Graph
          input/output schema binding.
        </p>
      </li>
      <li>
        <h3>Validate data offline</h3>
        <p>
          Validate typed input, authorization evidence, initial state, and the
          closed audit event against one frozen JSON Schema 2020-12 registry.
        </p>
      </li>
      <li>
        <h3>Recheck durable truth</h3>
        <p>
          PostgreSQL independently verifies graph registration, entry nodes,
          checkpoint shape, database-time budget admissibility, and every
          immutable event/checkpoint projection.
        </p>
      </li>
    </ol>
    <p>
      Schema rejection, deadline expiry, graph drift, and an injected late
      transaction failure leave no run, event, checkpoint, admission, or
      scheduler residue.
    </p>
  </section>

  <section aria-labelledby="security-title">
    <h2 id="security-title">Protect the admission snapshot</h2>
    <p>
      Admission bytes may contain user input, trusted instructions, principal
      attributes, authorization evidence, and policy limits. Use least-privilege
      roles, verified TLS, encrypted backups, tenant isolation, access auditing,
      and an explicit retention policy. Digests prove identity; they do not
      authenticate a principal or make data secret. The first journal event is
      deliberately public-safe correlation metadata only.
    </p>
  </section>

  <section aria-labelledby="evidence-title">
    <h2 id="evidence-title">Qualification evidence</h2>
    <p>
      The PostgreSQL 16/17 matrix now runs 102 provider cases and 26 durable
      runtime scenarios per version. Admission coverage includes migration 15,
      exact retry after time-sensitive boundaries, changed-intent and tamper
      rejection, invalid-state rollback with zero residue, 24-way convergence,
      and runtime rejection of Agent/Graph or authorization-schema drift before
      any write. Read the <a
        href="https://github.com/StateKnot/StateKnot/blob/main/docs/durable-agent-admission.md"
        >complete integration and rollout contract</a
      > before adopting this unpublished surface.
    </p>
  </section>
</DocsLayout>
